# Swagger Conventions (Non-Negotiable)

Every API endpoint MUST appear in Swagger UI with **sample request** and **sample response** always visible.

Stack: **Swashbuckle.AspNetCore** + **Swashbuckle.AspNetCore.Filters** (dev only).

Swagger UI URL (Development): `http://localhost:{port}/swagger`

## Every Endpoint Checklist

Before an endpoint is considered done:

- [ ] **Response DTO** — `public sealed record` in `Contracts/Responses/` (or feature folder)
- [ ] **Request DTO** — for POST/PUT/PATCH only, in `Contracts/Requests/`
- [ ] **Response example** — class implementing `IExamplesProvider<TResponse>` in `Contracts/Examples/`
- [ ] **Request example** — class implementing `IExamplesProvider<TRequest>` (body endpoints only)
- [ ] **`.Produces<TResponse>(status)`** — declares response schema to Swashbuckle
- [ ] **`.Produces<ProblemDetails>(400)`** and **`.Produces<ProblemDetails>(500)`** — error shapes
- [ ] **`.Accepts<TRequest>("application/json")`** — for body endpoints
- [ ] **`.WithMetadata(new SwaggerResponseExampleAttribute(...))`** — wires example into UI
- [ ] **`.WithMetadata(new SwaggerRequestExampleAttribute(...))`** — wires request example (body endpoints)
- [ ] **`.WithName()`** and **`.WithTags("module-name")`** — consistent grouping in Swagger

GET endpoints: response example required. No request body example needed.

## File Layout (Host + future modules)

```text
juskel.Api/
├── Contracts/
│   ├── Requests/
│   ├── Responses/
│   └── Examples/          # IExamplesProvider<T> classes
├── Program.cs
```

Inside modules (`identity.Core/Features/...`), colocate DTOs + Examples in the same vertical slice folder.

## Example Pattern

```csharp
// Contracts/Responses/RootResponse.cs
public sealed record RootResponse(string Status, string Version);

// Contracts/Examples/RootResponseExample.cs
public sealed class RootResponseExample : IExamplesProvider<RootResponse>
{
    public RootResponse GetExamples() => new("Online", "1.0.0");
}

// Program.cs
app.MapGet("/", () => Results.Ok(new RootResponse("Online", "1.0.0")))
    .WithName("GetRoot")
    .WithTags("system")
    .Produces<RootResponse>(StatusCodes.Status200OK)
    .Produces<ProblemDetails>(StatusCodes.Status500InternalServerError)
    .WithMetadata(new SwaggerResponseExampleAttribute(StatusCodes.Status200OK, typeof(RootResponseExample)));
```

POST pattern:

```csharp
app.MapPost("/applications", HandleCreate)
    .WithName("CreateApplication")
    .WithTags("funding")
    .Accepts<CreateApplicationRequest>("application/json")
    .Produces<CreateApplicationResponse>(StatusCodes.Status201Created)
    .Produces<ProblemDetails>(StatusCodes.Status400BadRequest)
    .Produces<ProblemDetails>(StatusCodes.Status500InternalServerError)
    .WithMetadata(new SwaggerRequestExampleAttribute(typeof(CreateApplicationRequest), typeof(CreateApplicationRequestExample)))
    .WithMetadata(new SwaggerResponseExampleAttribute(StatusCodes.Status201Created, typeof(CreateApplicationResponseExample)));
```

## Agent Duty

- Never add an endpoint without DTOs + example providers.
- Never use anonymous types (`new { status = ... }`) in endpoints — they produce weak/no examples in Swagger.
- Reject PRs or suggestions that skip `.Produces<>()` or example classes.
- Swagger is **Development only** — do not enable in Production (cost + security).
